# "Look at the top X cards" with X = twice the lands Bot1 controls. With no lands on turn 1 X is 0, there is nothing to look
# at and no question is asked (a refusal; the next cast is the control that asks). On turn 3, with two lands, X is 4 but the
# library holds only two cards (the Lotus was drawn), so Bot1 looks at those two and takes the Mountain, the Island going
# to the bottom. Two Moxen pay {B}{G} both times.

[Bot1 Deck]
Pillage the Bog
Pillage the Bog
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Swamp
Forest
Island
Black Lotus
Island
Mountain

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Pillage the Bog.Cast
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Arrange
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Pillage the Bog
? Bot1.Library.Count = 3
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Pillage the Bog.Cast
Bot1.Arrange(Mountain | Island)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Pillage the Bog; Pillage the Bog
Bot1.Library.Count = 1
Bot1.Hand = Black Lotus; Island; Mountain
